{"success":true,"thread_id":"trip_to_nepal_5days","answer":"### 5-Day Travel Itinerary: India to Nepal\n\n**Trip Overview:**\n- **Destination:** Nepal\n- **Origin:** India\n- **Duration:** 5 Days\n- **Travel Style:** Sightseeing and Adventure\n- **Special Preferences:** Adventure Activities\n\n---\n\n### Day 1: Arrival in Kathmandu\n\n**Morning:**\n- **Flight to Kathmandu:** Depart from your city in India (e.g., Delhi, Kolkata) to Tribhuvan International Airport, Kathmandu. Book a morning flight for a full day in Kathmandu.\n  \n**Afternoon:**\n- **Check-in:** Choose accommodation in Thamel, a vibrant area known for its shops, restaurants, and easy access to major attractions. Recommended hotels include Hotel Thamel, Hotel Manaslu, or similar budget-friendly options.\n- **Lunch:** Enjoy traditional Nepali cuisine at a local restaurant (try Momo or Dal Bhat).\n\n**Evening:**\n- **Sightseeing:** Visit Swayambhunath Stupa (Monkey Temple) for panoramic views of the city and a glimpse of the local culture.\n- **Dinner:** Dine at a rooftop restaurant in Thamel with views of the city.\n\n---\n\n### Day 2: Explore Kathmandu\n\n**Morning:**\n- **Sightseeing:** Visit Pashupatinath Temple, a UNESCO World Heritage Site, and observe the rituals along the Bagmati River.\n  \n**Afternoon:**\n- **Lunch:** Try a local eatery near the temple.\n- **Sightseeing:** Head to Boudhanath Stupa, one of the largest stupas in Nepal, and explore the surrounding area.\n\n**Evening:**\n- **Adventure Activity:** Join a guided evening hike to Nagarkot (about 1.5 hours from Kathmandu) for sunset views. \n- **Dinner:** Enjoy dinner at a local restaurant in Nagarkot.\n\n---\n\n### Day 3: Adventure in Pokhara\n\n**Morning:**\n- **Travel to Pokhara:** Early morning drive or take a domestic flight to Pokhara (approximately 6-7 hours by road or 30 minutes by air).\n- **Check-in:** Stay at a lakeside hotel like Hotel Lakefront or similar.\n\n**Afternoon:**\n- **Lunch:** Enjoy lunch at a lakeside café.\n- **Sightseeing:** Visit the World Peace Pagoda for stunning views of Pokhara and Phewa Lake.\n\n**Evening:**\n- **Adventure Activity:** Go paragliding over Phewa Lake for an exhilarating experience (book in advance).\n- **Dinner:** Enjoy a meal at a restaurant with local and international cuisine.\n\n---\n\n### Day 4: Adventure Activities in Pokhara\n\n**Morning:**\n- **Adventure Activity:** Go white-water rafting on the Seti River. This is a thrilling experience suitable for beginners and experienced rafters alike.\n  \n**Afternoon:**\n- **Lunch:** Have lunch at a local restaurant after your rafting adventure.\n- **Sightseeing:** Visit Devi’s Fall and Gupteshwor Cave.\n\n**Evening:**\n- **Leisure Time:** Explore the lakeside area, shop for souvenirs, or relax by the lake.\n- **Dinner:** Try a local restaurant for traditional Nepali food.\n\n---\n\n### Day 5: Return to Kathmandu and Departure\n\n**Morning:**\n- **Travel Back to Kathmandu:** Depart early from Pokhara to Kathmandu (by flight or road).\n  \n**Afternoon:**\n- **Last-minute Sightseeing:** If time permits, visit the Kathmandu Durbar Square and explore the local shops.\n- **Lunch:** Enjoy a final meal in Kathmandu.\n\n**Evening:**\n- **Departure:** Head to Tribhuvan International Airport for your flight back to India.\n\n---\n\n### Accommodation Suggestions (Non-Live Advice)\n\n- **Kathmandu:** \n  - Hotel Thamel\n  - Hotel Manaslu\n  - Hotel Shanker\n\n- **Pokhara:** \n  - Hotel Lakefront\n  - Fish Tail Lodge\n  - Temple Tree Resort & Spa\n\n### Budget Tips:\n- **Flights:** Book in advance for better rates.\n- **Local Transport:** Use local buses or shared taxis for budget-friendly travel.\n- **Meals:** Eat at local restaurants to save money and enjoy authentic cuisine.\n- **Activities:** Look for package deals for adventure activities.\n\n### Important Notes:\n- Ensure you have a valid passport and any necessary visas for entry into Nepal.\n- Check for any travel advisories or health requirements before your trip.\n- Consider travel insurance for adventure activities.\n\nEnjoy your adventure-filled trip to Nepal!","requires_approval":true,"approval_request":"Please review the generated draft itinerary. Approve it to create the final polished plan, or provide feedback for revision.","flight_results":"Flight information unavailable: asyncio.run() cannot be called from a running event loop","hotel_results":"Live hotel search is temporarily unavailable. Provide general accommodation and neighborhood guidance based on the destination and clearly label it as non-live advice.","budget_results":"","itinerary":"### 5-Day Travel Itinerary: India to Nepal\n\n**Trip Overview:**\n- **Destination:** Nepal\n- **Origin:** India\n- **Duration:** 5 Days\n- **Travel Style:** Sightseeing and Adventure\n- **Special Preferences:** Adventure Activities\n\n---\n\n### Day 1: Arrival in Kathmandu\n\n**Morning:**\n- **Flight to Kathmandu:** Depart from your city in India (e.g., Delhi, Kolkata) to Tribhuvan International Airport, Kathmandu. Book a morning flight for a full day in Kathmandu.\n  \n**Afternoon:**\n- **Check-in:** Choose accommodation in Thamel, a vibrant area known for its shops, restaurants, and easy access to major attractions. Recommended hotels include Hotel Thamel, Hotel Manaslu, or similar budget-friendly options.\n- **Lunch:** Enjoy traditional Nepali cuisine at a local restaurant (try Momo or Dal Bhat).\n\n**Evening:**\n- **Sightseeing:** Visit Swayambhunath Stupa (Monkey Temple) for panoramic views of the city and a glimpse of the local culture.\n- **Dinner:** Dine at a rooftop restaurant in Thamel with views of the city.\n\n---\n\n### Day 2: Explore Kathmandu\n\n**Morning:**\n- **Sightseeing:** Visit Pashupatinath Temple, a UNESCO World Heritage Site, and observe the rituals along the Bagmati River.\n  \n**Afternoon:**\n- **Lunch:** Try a local eatery near the temple.\n- **Sightseeing:** Head to Boudhanath Stupa, one of the largest stupas in Nepal, and explore the surrounding area.\n\n**Evening:**\n- **Adventure Activity:** Join a guided evening hike to Nagarkot (about 1.5 hours from Kathmandu) for sunset views. \n- **Dinner:** Enjoy dinner at a local restaurant in Nagarkot.\n\n---\n\n### Day 3: Adventure in Pokhara\n\n**Morning:**\n- **Travel to Pokhara:** Early morning drive or take a domestic flight to Pokhara (approximately 6-7 hours by road or 30 minutes by air).\n- **Check-in:** Stay at a lakeside hotel like Hotel Lakefront or similar.\n\n**Afternoon:**\n- **Lunch:** Enjoy lunch at a lakeside café.\n- **Sightseeing:** Visit the World Peace Pagoda for stunning views of Pokhara and Phewa Lake.\n\n**Evening:**\n- **Adventure Activity:** Go paragliding over Phewa Lake for an exhilarating experience (book in advance).\n- **Dinner:** Enjoy a meal at a restaurant with local and international cuisine.\n\n---\n\n### Day 4: Adventure Activities in Pokhara\n\n**Morning:**\n- **Adventure Activity:** Go white-water rafting on the Seti River. This is a thrilling experience suitable for beginners and experienced rafters alike.\n  \n**Afternoon:**\n- **Lunch:** Have lunch at a local restaurant after your rafting adventure.\n- **Sightseeing:** Visit Devi’s Fall and Gupteshwor Cave.\n\n**Evening:**\n- **Leisure Time:** Explore the lakeside area, shop for souvenirs, or relax by the lake.\n- **Dinner:** Try a local restaurant for traditional Nepali food.\n\n---\n\n### Day 5: Return to Kathmandu and Departure\n\n**Morning:**\n- **Travel Back to Kathmandu:** Depart early from Pokhara to Kathmandu (by flight or road).\n  \n**Afternoon:**\n- **Last-minute Sightseeing:** If time permits, visit the Kathmandu Durbar Square and explore the local shops.\n- **Lunch:** Enjoy a final meal in Kathmandu.\n\n**Evening:**\n- **Departure:** Head to Tribhuvan International Airport for your flight back to India.\n\n---\n\n### Accommodation Suggestions (Non-Live Advice)\n\n- **Kathmandu:** \n  - Hotel Thamel\n  - Hotel Manaslu\n  - Hotel Shanker\n\n- **Pokhara:** \n  - Hotel Lakefront\n  - Fish Tail Lodge\n  - Temple Tree Resort & Spa\n\n### Budget Tips:\n- **Flights:** Book in advance for better rates.\n- **Local Transport:** Use local buses or shared taxis for budget-friendly travel.\n- **Meals:** Eat at local restaurants to save money and enjoy authentic cuisine.\n- **Activities:** Look for package deals for adventure activities.\n\n### Important Notes:\n- Ensure you have a valid passport and any necessary visas for entry into Nepal.\n- Check for any travel advisories or health requirements before your trip.\n- Consider travel insurance for adventure activities.\n\nEnjoy your adventure-filled trip to Nepal!","selected_agents":["flight_agent","hotel_agent","itinerary_agent"],"trip_constraints":{"destination":"Nepal","origin":"India","duration":"5 days","budget":"","travel_style":"sightseeing and adventure","special_preferences":["adventure activities"]},"supervisor_reasoning":"The request involves planning a trip that includes flights, accommodation, and a detailed itinerary for sightseeing and adventure activities, necessitating the inclusion of the flight_agent, hotel_agent, and itinerary_agent.","guardrail_allowed":true,"guardrail_reason":"The request involves travel planning, including destinations, sightseeing, and adventure activities.","approved":false,"human_feedback":"","llm_calls":5}